// THE TWO NUMBERS SHARE A BASELINE AND DO NOT SHARE A WEIGHT. The price is the
// subject; the delta is an annotation on it, so it is smaller, lighter and set
// in the direction's colour rather than sitting beside the price as a second
// figure of equal standing -- which is exactly the failure the two-column
// `Market` / `Live value` pair had.
//
// `baseline`, not `center`: the delta is a size smaller than the price, and
// centred the smaller type floats visibly above the dollar sign.
//
// The size of the price itself is NOT set here. It comes from
// `.selected__player-header-item` in selected-player.styl, which both call
// sites carry -- and note that rule sets 18px on the ITEM, so it wins over the
// 12px `.nominated__player-details` sets on the auction bar's group around it.
// Measured, the price renders 18px on both surfaces. This component is a value
// in someone else's row, not a row of its own.
//
// THE PRICE IS CENTRED UNDER THE LABEL AND THE DELTA HANGS OFF IT, which is
// what the three-track grid buys and a flex row cannot. Flexed, the pair is
// centred as a UNIT, so the price sits left of centre by half the delta's width
// and MOVES as the delta changes -- `$7` under `MARKET VALUE` is at one x
// position with no inflation, another at `+$2`, another at `+$12`. The label is
// the fixed thing on this item and the price is what the reader looks for under
// it, so the price is what has to hold still.
//
// `1fr auto 1fr`: the price takes the middle track, the delta the third, and
// the first is empty. Equal flex factors make the two `fr` tracks the same
// width whichever way the item is sized -- they split the surplus when the
// label is the wider thing, and when the delta is wider than the surplus they
// both grow to it, since an `fr` track floors at its own content. Either way
// the outer pair match, so the middle track is centred by construction and the
// price never moves. `justify-self start` keeps the delta against the price
// rather than centred in a track that may be wider than it.
//
// `align-self stretch`, because a centred track is only centred within the
// width it was given. `.selected__player-header-item` is a centring flex COLUMN
// (selected-player.styl), so a child sizes to its own content by default and
// this grid would span the price alone -- centring it inside itself, which is
// no constraint at all. Stretched, the grid spans the item, and the item's
// width is the label's.
.player__auction-value-amounts
  display grid
  grid-template-columns 1fr auto 1fr
  align-self stretch
  align-items baseline

.player__auction-value-amount
  grid-column 2

.player__auction-value-inflation
  grid-column 3
  justify-self start
  padding-left 5px

// `em`, so the delta tracks whatever size the surrounding row set for the
// price. Fixed at 11px it read as an annotation in the 12px auction bar and as
// a footnote against the drawer's 18px.
//
// COLOUR IS THE ONLY THING CARRYING THE DIRECTION at a glance -- the sign is
// one character -- so the sign is rendered as well and the colour reinforces it
// rather than being the whole message.
//
// $successColor for over-market and a lightened $textColor for under. NOT red
// for under: red is $accentColor, and the auction bar spends it on the standing
// election a few inches away, so an under-market delta in red would read as an
// alert about the bid rather than as a direction.
.player__auction-value-inflation
  font-size 0.72em
  font-weight 500
  &.over
    color $successColor
  &.under
    color lighten($textColor, 25)
